  "summary": "When I was a kid I had a running list of inventions I was working on in my head. They included large machine, specifically tanks  Becoming a computer engineer my way of following my dream to become an inventor.  I get to participate with other creative minds in bringing ideas into reality.  \n\nI believe that employees that collaborate well together and are \"all in\" are a company's greatest asset.  I'm passionate about bringing new ideas to fruition and making them faster, better and smaller.\n\nI currently work as a software engineer at Komatsu America.  I am a graduate in Computer Engineering from Utah State University, one of the top engineering schools in the country.\n\nIn my current position, I participate in all stages of the Software development cycle, working closely with a collaborative team  I have strong programming skills in multiple languages, including more than five years of experience programming in C and C++, and years of professional experience with LabVIEW as well as strong skills in Python, Nodejs, and other languages",
